{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato","suddhaso"],"title":"21. Miscellaneous","html":"<section class='range'  id='dhp290-305'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Khuddakanikāya </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Minor Collection </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Collection of Minor Texts </span></li>\n<li class='subdivision'><span class='root'>Dhammapada </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Sayings of the Dhamma 290–305 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Verses of Dhamma </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='range-title'><span class='root'>Pakiṇṇakavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>21. Miscellaneous </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>The Scattered Chapter </span></h1></header>\n<article id='dhp290'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Attanopubbakammavatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Mattāsukhapariccāgā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>If by giving up material happiness </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>If by relinquishing limited happiness </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>passe ce vipulaṁ sukhaṁ; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>one sees abundant happiness, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>one can see abundant happiness, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Caje mattāsukhaṁ dhīro, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>the attentive would give up material happiness, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>then one who is wise relinquishes limited happiness </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>sampassaṁ vipulaṁ sukhaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>seeing the abundant happiness. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>and sees abundant happiness. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp291'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Kukkuṭaṇḍakhādikāvatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Paradukkhūpadhānena, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Seeking their own happiness </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>By profiting from the suffering of others, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>attano sukhamicchati; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>by imposing suffering on others, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>one seeks happiness for oneself; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Verasaṁsaggasaṁsaṭṭho, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>intimate with enmity, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>one who is intimately involved in hostility </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>verā so na parimuccati. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>they’re not freed from enmity. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>is not free from hostility. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp292'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Bhaddiyānaṁbhikkhūnaṁvatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Yañhi kiccaṁ apaviddhaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>They dump what should be done, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>They reject what should be done </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>akiccaṁ pana karīyati; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>and do what should not be done. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>and do what should not be done; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Unnaḷānaṁ pamattānaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>For the insolent and the negligent, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>arrogant and negligent, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>tesaṁ vaḍḍhanti āsavā. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>their defilements only grow. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>their defilements increase. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp293'><blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Yesañca susamāraddhā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Those that have properly undertaken </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>They have undertaken </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>niccaṁ kāyagatā sati; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>constant mindfulness of the body, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>continuous mindfulness of the body, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Akiccaṁ te na sevanti, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>don’t cultivate what should not be done, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>they do not do what should not be done, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>kicce sātaccakārino; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>but always do what should be done. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>and they always do what should be done; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Satānaṁ sampajānānaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Mindful and aware, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>mindful and aware, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>atthaṁ gacchanti āsavā. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>their defilements come to an end. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>their defilements disappear. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp294'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Lakuṇḍakabhaddiyavatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Mātaraṁ pitaraṁ hantvā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Having slain mother and father, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Having slain mother and father, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>rājāno dve ca khattiye; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>and two aristocratic kings, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>two royal kings, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Raṭṭhaṁ sānucaraṁ hantvā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>and having wiped out <j>the kingdom with its tax collector, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>and a kingdom with its followers, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>anīgho yāti brāhmaṇo. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>the brahmin walks on untroubled. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>the brahmin proceeds untroubled. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp295'><blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Mātaraṁ pitaraṁ hantvā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Having slain mother and father, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Having slain mother and father, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>rājāno dve ca sotthiye; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>and two prosperous kings, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>two scholar kings, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Veyagghapañcamaṁ hantvā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>and a tiger as the fifth, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>and a tiger as well, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>anīgho yāti brāhmaṇo. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>the brahmin walks on untroubled. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>the brahmin proceeds untroubled. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp296'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Dārusākaṭikaputtavatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Suppabuddhaṁ pabujjhanti, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The disciples of Gotama </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>They always wake up well, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>sadā gotamasāvakā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>always wake up refreshed, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>the disciples of Gotama </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Yesaṁ divā ca ratto ca, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>who day and night </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>who continuously recollect the Buddha </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>niccaṁ buddhagatā sati. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>constantly recollect the Buddha. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>by day and by night. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp297'><blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Suppabuddhaṁ pabujjhanti, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The disciples of Gotama </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>They always wake up well, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>sadā gotamasāvakā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>always wake up refreshed, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>disciples of the Buddha </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Yesaṁ divā ca ratto ca, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>who day and night </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>who continuously recollect the Dhamma </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>niccaṁ dhammagatā sati. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>constantly recollect the teaching. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>by day and by night. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp298'><blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Suppabuddhaṁ pabujjhanti, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The disciples of Gotama </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>They always wake up well, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>sadā gotamasāvakā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>always wake up refreshed, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>the disciples of Gotama </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Yesaṁ divā ca ratto ca, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>who day and night </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>who continuously recollect the Saṅgha </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>niccaṁ saṅghagatā sati. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>constantly recollect the Saṅgha. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>by day and by night. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp299'><blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Suppabuddhaṁ pabujjhanti, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The disciples of Gotama </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>They always wake up well, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>sadā gotamasāvakā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>always wake up refreshed, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>the disciples of Gotama </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Yesaṁ divā ca ratto ca, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>who day and night </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>who continuously practice mindfulness of the body </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>niccaṁ kāyagatā sati. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>are constantly mindful of the body. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>by day and by night. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp300'><blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Suppabuddhaṁ pabujjhanti, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The disciples of Gotama </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>They always wake up well, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>sadā gotamasāvakā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>always wake up refreshed, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>the disciples of Gotama </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Yesaṁ divā ca ratto ca, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>whose minds day and night </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>who approve of harmlessness </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>ahiṁsāya rato mano. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>delight in harmlessness. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>by day and by night. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp301'><blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Suppabuddhaṁ pabujjhanti, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The disciples of Gotama </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>They always wake up well, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>sadā gotamasāvakā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>always wake up refreshed, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>the disciples of Gotama </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Yesaṁ divā ca ratto ca, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>whose minds day and night </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>who approve of self-development </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>bhāvanāya rato mano. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>delight in meditation. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>by day and by night. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp302'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Vajjiputtakabhikkhuvatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Duppabbajjaṁ durabhiramaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Going forth is hard, it’s hard to be happy; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>The renunciant life is difficult and hard to enjoy; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Durāvāsā gharā dukhā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>life at home is hard too, and painful, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>the household life is difficult and hard to endure. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Dukkhosamānasaṁvāso, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>it’s painful to stay when you’ve nothing in common. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Living with others is suffering, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Dukkhānupatitaddhagū; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>A traveler is a prey to pain, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>and travelers also undergo suffering. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Tasmā na caddhagū siyā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>so don’t be a traveler, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Therefore, just as one can choose to not travel, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Na ca dukkhānupatito siyā. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>don’t be prey to pain. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>one can choose to not suffer. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp303'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Cittagahapativatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Saddho sīlena sampanno, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>One who is faithful, accomplished in ethics, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>One who has faith and morality, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>yasobhogasamappito; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>blessed with fame and wealth, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>influence and wealth, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Yaṁ yaṁ padesaṁ bhajati, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>is honored in whatever place </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>is honored </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>tattha tattheva pūjito. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>they frequent. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>wherever they are. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp304'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Cūḷasubhaddāvatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Dūre santo pakāsenti, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The good shine from afar, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Those who are good are visible from afar, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>himavantova pabbato; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>like the Himalayan peaks, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>like a Himalayan mountain; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Asantettha na dissanti, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>but the wicked are not seen, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>but those who are not good cannot be seen, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>rattiṁ khittā yathā sarā. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>like arrows scattered in the night. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>like arrows loosed at night. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp305'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Ekavihārittheravatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Ekāsanaṁ ekaseyyaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Sitting alone, sleeping alone, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Sitting alone, sleeping alone, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>eko caramatandito; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>tirelessly wandering alone; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>going alone, never lazy; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Eko damayamattānaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>one who tames themselves alone </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>training oneself alone, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>vanante ramito siyā. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>would delight within a forest. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>one can enjoy the forest. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endvagga'><span class='root'>Pakiṇṇakavaggo ekavīsatimo. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></p></article></section>"}
